From fc9bb4d82401410b50d63799f425474be75506d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:37:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 404/417] Unified: a rough MuJoCo model (MJCF) of an assembly

--export-mjcf model.xml [--mjcf-mesh] (MjcfExport.export): the parts as
bodies with mass, centre of mass and inertia from the solids (material
density, else 7850 kg/m3; FreeCAD's Default material of 1 kg/m3 is no
material), a box each for contacts with the surroundings (not with each
other: an engine's boxes overlap and jammed the crank), meshes for the
looks (coarse binary STL). From the grounded parts and the assembly's
origin the joints are followed: hinges, slides, balls; a joint closing a
loop as <equality connect>; belts and gears as a ratio of the two hinges
(teeth, else radii; the sign from the hinges' axes). An engine exports
in 12 s and turns in MuJoCo with the camshaft at half the crank.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
